Say WHO put the text in, not just which storage got it.

CIDER_TEXTEDIT already fired on every mutation of every text storage and named the storage and the
resulting length, which is what proved that exactly one of iA Writer's three editor storages ever
receives the document. It could not say HOW the characters arrived, and #194 needed that: the
application never calls -[IAEditorViewController setText:annotations:], measured with the probe
armed as "taking @ and @ returning v" and its two neighbours firing in the same run, so the route
could not be assumed.

Two return address frames, the same pair CIDER_TRACE_FRAMES uses and for the same reason: the
nearest caller is usually a forwarding method of ours and the interesting one is whoever called
THAT.

It answered on the first run. The 40 characters reach the editor storage through

  mask=0x3 range=0+0 delta=40 len=40
      from replaceCharactersInRangeWithAttributedString
      <- -[NSTextStorage_concrete replaceCharactersInRange:withAttributedString:]
  mask=0x2 range=0+40 delta=0 len=40
      from -[IATextController parser:willStartParsingInRange:]
      <- -[IAMarkdownLiveParser willStartInRange:]

so the text is inserted normally AND iA Writer runs its own markdown live parser over it. The text
side is working. The editor holding it is simply not the one in the window.

The same trace also separates the editor storages from the one NSStringDrawer shares for menu and
label drawing, which accounts for most of the traffic and is not a text view at all.

--- a/AppKit/NSTextView.subproj/NSTextStorage.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSTextView.subproj/NSTextStorage.m
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #import <AppKit/NSLayoutManager.h>
 #import <AppKit/NSTextStorage.h>
 #import <objc/runtime.h>
+#import <dlfcn.h>
 #import <Foundation/NSKeyedArchiver.h>
 
 NSString *const NSTextStorageWillProcessEditingNotification =
@@ -229,9 +230,23 @@
      * different storage from the one the application filled, and the POINTER is what separates
      * those. Task #194. */
     if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_TEXT") != NULL && getenv("CIDER_TRACE_TEXT")[0] != (char) 0) {
-        fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_TEXTEDIT %s(%p) mask=0x%x range=%lu+%lu delta=%d len=%lu\n",
+        /* WHO PUT THE TEXT IN. Knowing WHICH storage got text left #194 one question short: iA
+         * Writer never calls -[IAEditorViewController setText:annotations:], measured with the
+         * probe armed and its neighbours firing, so the route the characters take has to be read
+         * off the stack rather than guessed at. Two frames, because the nearest caller is usually
+         * a forwarding method of ours and the interesting one is whoever called THAT. */
+        Dl_info info, infoUp;
+        void *ret = __builtin_return_address(0);
+        void *retUp = __builtin_return_address(1);
+
+        fprintf(stderr,
+                "CIDER_TEXTEDIT %s(%p) mask=0x%x range=%lu+%lu delta=%d len=%lu from %s <- %s\n",
                 object_getClassName(self), self, editedMask, (unsigned long) range.location,
-                (unsigned long) range.length, delta, (unsigned long) [self length]);
+                (unsigned long) range.length, delta, (unsigned long) [self length],
+                (dladdr(ret, &info) != 0 && info.dli_sname != NULL) ? info.dli_sname : "?",
+                (retUp != NULL && dladdr(retUp, &infoUp) != 0 && infoUp.dli_sname != NULL)
+                        ? infoUp.dli_sname
+                        : "?");
         fflush(stderr);
     }
 
